#   compiler        g++ (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0, -O2 -g -DNDEBUG
#   core            THE shared ak-core at ffi/poc/codec (R0), cdylib and staticlib
#   rustc           rustc 1.94.1 (e408947bf 2026-03-25)
#   oracle          protobuf C++ 3.21.12, pb_serialize_det -- an encoder no plant can reach
#   shapes          P1.1 (858 B), P1.3 (605 B, the absent path), P1.2 (218 KB), P2.2 (540 KB)
#   commit          b6479775 + the working tree this log was taken from

12.5 was, in the corpus agent's words, the obligation with the most evidence behind it
and the least existence. No slice had one. This is the C++ side of it: two axes
(threads in sequence and threads together), four payload shapes across two message
types, every encode memcmp'd against a reference, and -- because a suite that has only
ever passed has not been seen working -- three PLANTED builds of the two designs ABI v1
section 6 refused, each of which the suite must catch.

== ABI v1 obligation 12.5 ==
nproc = 4

